The categories $\mathcal P(\varphi)$ form a slicing of $\mathcal D$ with finite Harder–Narasimhan filtrations. They satisfy $$\label{eq:slicing-covariance}
 \mathcal P(\varphi+1)=\mathcal P(\varphi)[1],\qquad
 \Phi\mathcal P(\varphi)=\mathcal P(\varphi+2/5)
 \quad(\varphi\in\mathbb R),$$ and every nonzero $E\in\mathcal P(\varphi)$ satisfies $$\label{eq:semistable-support}
 Z(E)\in\mathbb R_{>0}e^{i\pi\varphi},\qquad
 \left\lVert[E]\right\rVert\le C|Z(E)|.$$

