The map $v$ identifies $K_{\mathrm{num}}(X)_{\mathbb R}$ with $\mathbb R^4$. Under this identification, $K_{\mathrm{num}}(X)$ is a full discrete lattice contained in $$\label{eq:numerical-lattice}
 \mathbb Z\times\mathbb Z\times\tfrac1{10}\mathbb Z\times\tfrac1{30}\mathbb Z.$$ For $v=(r,c,d,e)$ and $w=(r',c',d',e')$, the Euler form is $$\label{eq:euler-form}
 \chi(v,w)=5\left(re'-cd'+dc'-er'
                   +\frac56(rc'-cr')\right).$$ The matrix induced by $\Phi$ is $$\label{eq:numerical-rotation}
 M=
 \begin{pmatrix}
 -4&-20/3&-5&-5\\
 1&1&0&0\\
 1/2&1&1&0\\
 1/6&1/2&1&1
 \end{pmatrix},
 \qquad
 \det(zI-M)=z^4+z^3+z^2+z+1.$$

There is a unique numerical homomorphism $Z\colon K_{\mathrm{num}}(X)\to\mathbb C$ such that $Z\circ\Phi=\lambda Z$ and $Z(\mathcal O_x)=-1$ for closed points $x\in X$. It is $$\label{eq:central-charge}
 \frac{Z(r,c,d,e)}5
  =\frac{\lambda-1}{5}r
   +\left(t_0^2-\frac56+\frac{i t_0}{2}\right)c
   +\left(-\frac12+i t_0\right)d-e.$$ In particular, $$\label{eq:imaginary-charge}
 \frac{\operatorname{Im}Z(r,c,d,e)}{5t_0}=d+\frac12c+ur.$$ For any fixed norm on $K_{\mathrm{num}}(X)_{\mathbb R}$, there is a constant $C_0>0$ such that every real numerical class $v=(r,c,d,e)$ satisfies $$\label{eq:numerical-norm-control}
 \left\lVert v\right\rVert\le C_0\bigl(|r|+|c|+|Z(v)|\bigr).$$

Put $$f(x)=\max\left\{-\frac{3x}{25},\ \frac{x}{2}-\frac7{25},\
                    \frac{28x}{25}-\frac{31}{50}\right\}
                    \qquad(0\leq x\leq1).$$ Every torsion-free slope-semistable sheaf $F$ on $X$ with $|\mu(F)|\leq1$ satisfies $$\label{eq:slope-envelope}
                 \frac{d(F)}{r(F)}\leq f(|\mu(F)|).$$ The estimate extends under integral twists by $(x,y)\mapsto(x+n,y+nx+n^2/2)$. In particular, $f(x)\leq0$ for $0\leq x\leq1/2$, and $f(1/2)=-3/100$.

There is a fixed open square $$\label{eq:fixed-omega}
 \Omega=\{\eta=(\eta_0,\eta_1):|\eta_0|,|\eta_1|<5\cdot10^{-6}\}$$ and bounded aisles $U_\eta=\mathcal U_-^\eta$, with hearts $\mathcal A_\eta=U_\eta\cap(U_\eta[1])^\perp$, such that $$\label{eq:uniform-aisle}
                    \Phi U_\eta\subset U_\theta
                    \qquad(\eta,\theta\in\Omega).$$ Moreover $$\label{eq:perturbed-positive-form}
 N_\eta=d+\frac12c+ur+\eta_1c+\eta_0r\geq0
                    \quad\text{on }\mathcal A_\eta,
 \qquad N_0=\frac{\operatorname{Im}Z}{5t_0},$$ and no nonzero object of any $\mathcal A_\eta$ has zero numerical class. The two parameters in <a href="#eq:uniform-aisle" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:uniform-aisle">[eq:uniform-aisle]</a> vary independently throughout this same square.

There is an open square $\Omega_1$ about zero, contained in $\Omega$, such that $$\label{eq:single-shift-inclusion}
 D_3^\alpha\subset D_0^\beta[1]
 \qquad(\alpha,\beta\in\Omega_1).$$ For $k\in\mathbb Z$ and $\eta\in\Omega_1$, define $$\label{eq:fifths-aisles}
 V_k^\eta=\Phi^mU_\eta[j],\qquad k=2m+5j.$$ This is independent of the integers $m,j$ chosen, and these bounded aisles satisfy $$\label{eq:fifths-nesting}
 \begin{gathered}
 V_{k+1}^\alpha\subset V_k^\beta,\qquad
 V_{k+5}^\eta=V_k^\eta[1],\qquad
 \Phi V_k^\eta=V_{k+2}^\eta,\\
 k\in\mathbb Z,\quad \alpha,\beta,\eta\in\Omega_1.
 \end{gathered}$$

For the fixed Euclidean norm on $K_{\mathrm{num}}(X)_\mathbb R$, there is a constant $C>0$ such that, for every $k\in\mathbb Z$ and every nonzero $E\in\mathcal S_k$, $$\label{eq:block-support}
 \begin{gathered}
 Z(E)\in\{t e^{i\pi\varphi}:t>0,\ k/5\le\varphi\le(k+1)/5\},\\
 \left\lVert[E]\right\rVert\le C|Z(E)|.
 \end{gathered}$$

The categories $\mathcal P(\varphi)$ form a slicing of $\mathcal D$ with finite Harder–Narasimhan filtrations. They satisfy $$\label{eq:slicing-covariance}
 \mathcal P(\varphi+1)=\mathcal P(\varphi)[1],\qquad
 \Phi\mathcal P(\varphi)=\mathcal P(\varphi+2/5)
 \quad(\varphi\in\mathbb R),$$ and every nonzero $E\in\mathcal P(\varphi)$ satisfies $$\label{eq:semistable-support}
 Z(E)\in\mathbb R_{>0}e^{i\pi\varphi},\qquad
 \left\lVert[E]\right\rVert\le C|Z(E)|.$$
